      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings are amplified, it sounds, but you're not alone in experiencing deep emotional pain, and many people go through similar struggles. It can be very lonely and frustrating when those close to us don't fully understand. I believe there is hope for things to get better, though it's a process that often takes time and sometimes professional help, like therapy, which can provide additional support and coping strategies to navigate through this difficult time. If you're comfortable, consider reconnecting with friends or family to share your feelings in depth. Also, it's important to practice self-care and to give yourself moments of tranquility whenever you can. If you ever feel ready, professional mental health services can be a safe place to start exploring what's going on and finding ways to work through it.",
